{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537430-v20-do-you-apply-stamina-soaking-specialties-to-soaking-rolls-involving-armor","id":1537430,"title":"[V20] Do you apply Stamina soaking specialties to soaking rolls involving Armor?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-15T14:09:58-07:00","id":1537430,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [V20] Do you apply Stamina soaking specialties to soaking rolls involving Armor?","content":"While the title is self-explanatory, I'll elaborate.<br /> Let's say you have Stamina 5, Fortitude 4, and you wear a Kevlar Vest (Armor Rating: 3, Dexterity Penalty -1).<br /> That a total of 12 dice.<br /> My question is if you also had a Stamina soaking specialty (e.g. Tough as Nails), you will consider it as a <b>single roll of 12 dice</b> and apply the Specialty benefits there?<br /> Or alternatively you will roll Stamina + Fortitude separately (9 dice) and apply the Specialty, and only then roll the Armor (3 dice) on its own without Specialty benefits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T16:08:15-07:00","id":1537433,"title":"","content":"I would apply as a single roll, for simplicity's sake if nothing else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T07:20:33-07:00","id":1537486,"title":"","content":"I understand. Question is how it was truly meant to be by the book?<br /> The thing is that I would argue that the Armor is technically an object, and has its own separate dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T08:53:00-07:00","id":1537493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537430-v20-do-you-apply-stamina-soaking-specialties-to-soaking-rolls-involving-armor?p=1537486#post1537486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand. Question is how it was truly meant to be by the book?<br /> The thing is that I would argue that the Armor is technically an object, and has its own separate dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK your question has no answer. The books never cared about distinguishing properly what is what on the soak roll, just what is included in the roll depending on the type and source of damage.<br /> <br /> None is particularly realistic, either. If you have an ability to endure better at certain situations, why wouldn't you be able to apply it both for your body and to how you use your equipment? IRL using defensive gear is a far more active thing than just a passive benefit.<br /> <br /> Either way I don't remember ever seeing any answer to this question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T16:27:11-07:00","id":1537532,"title":"","content":"The books have been frustratingly unclear about how to apply Specialties to damage, soak, and initiative.<br /> <br /> That said, if you're allowing a Stamina specialty to apply to Soak rolls, it applies to the one soak roll you make even if you get bonus dice from other sources. The books have never had specialties apply differently in such circumstances. There's no rule that indicates you have to break up a roll into multiple rolls over a specialty.<br /> <br /> Armor doesn't have a separate dice pool. Armor is a bonus to your dice-pool (even if your dice-pool starts at zero for those that can't soak without armor). When you roll damage with a melee weapon, you combine Strength, weapon damage, threshold successes, and other bonuses (like Potence) into one pool. The damage dice from how hard you hit, how well you hit, and what you hit with, are never differentiated after that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}